A||||11||Master_Sushi||I got in an accident,PLS help||||1||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||08-09-2000||11:02 PM||||God, I feel terrable. Well I was heading back from work tonight like I allways do. It was rainy and very fogy. I was pulling out into a quiet road (with a curb) as normal. Keep in mind im a very calm, responsable driver. Well I dont even know what happend from then on really. I jsut remember pulling out slowly like normal, except for the fact that my  tired let lose and were howeling. So I tried to control the skid, but no go. I hit the brakes. Then I was sliding all over the place. So I tried to control the skid, but no go.   And then I hit the curb with my right wheel, I msut have been doing 10 or 15. I dont know how this even happend, I wasnt screwing around or anything. I think its jsut my bald orignal hard tires. <P>It seems that this has really screwed up my steering, the steering wheel is spun way left. Also my right tire is pointed Left.<P>I really need help on this one guies! Is my car really screwed up? Or will an alignment fix it?? Or do I need the whole front suspension fixed?<P>I feel so sick from this whole thing happening...<P>Sorry for the long post.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||08-09-2000||11:51 PM||||But no one was hurt, right? (always a good thing..)<P>and if it's any consolation, I've accidentally put a car in a ditch before... backwards... (luckily the exhaust didn't get ripped off... just bent..)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000002||Uaana||08-10-2000||12:52 AM||||Glad to hear you are o.k.<BR>But from your brief description sounds like you may have bent/broken a tie rod. at the least. you won't know till you look under the car or pull your wheels off and check them. Like I said this is only a maybe cause your description was kinda brief.<BR>Good luck.<BR>Hope you have a better tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||08-10-2000||04:23 AM||||Dude, are you SURE nobody clipped you?<P>Anyways, skids like that can happen.  Especially if you hit a hole with some water in it. That's why I invested in extra-traction tires for rainy weather (like that's a problem in San Diego)!<P>My sister had damages similiar to it.  If I remember correctly she needed a new axle.  And her tire was only a bit pointed in.<P>But it could be a tie rod also.  Have it appraised and find out!<P>I'm truly sorry man, but be glad you didn't hit a pole or anything and you made it alive!  Cars are repairable, your life ain't!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||08-10-2000||10:03 AM||||<BR>I agree with Uaana, but there may be other damage, like a bent lower control arm.  You will not know the extent of the damage until you remove that wheel.<P>Take a photo or two and post them, may be we can be of further assistance.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||08-10-2000||10:13 AM||||I agree with the "bent tie rod" diagnosis.  You might have fragged your steering rack too, but it's less likely.  It's possible you could have bent the lower suspension arm, but I doubt it unless you hit the curb sliding totally sideways - the 84-87 suspension is pretty tough (I found out the hard way with my 84 - don't ask and I won't tell).<P>I doubt an alignment will fix it, but it shouldn't cost too awfully much to get you rolling again.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||08-10-2000||11:42 AM||||Well I went and took a look better at it this morning. I took the tire off and pojked around. I really am not much on suspension expert so about all I could do was make sure eerything looked ok. It all looked that same as when i changed the shocks last month, so Hopefully it nothing really bad. Im going to take it into an auto repair shop today and get a front end alignment, then go from there.<BR>The car is in perfect shape as I can tell other then the rim being scratched badly on the side. Its also not so bad that I cant drive it. It just pulls to the right pretty good. <P>But ill jsut have to see what the auto place says.<P>Thanks for all the help, without this forum id be lost!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Master_Sushi||08-10-2000||11:46 AM||||Oh ya, also noone was hurt in it. I didnt hit anyone, jsut the curb. Only thing hurt is my poor car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TheFiero64||08-10-2000||12:12 PM||||It sounds like tie-rod popped out and that caused the whole thing. That is why the tire is turned. It needs a new tie-rod end. This happened to a friend. The tie-rod ball pops out of the socket and the wheel turns and the car goes crazy.  <P>P.S. Glad you are alright<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000009||JohnnyK||08-10-2000||05:33 PM||||Agh.. What are teh chances of that happening? (It's another thing to worry about now. That, and my mystery weld)||||reg||1
Z||000010||fldevel||08-10-2000||11:45 PM||||at least  you dident do it on a dry road like i did .. i think i blame it on the dry cracked 225/60 r-14 i was running on it ..anyway i was going around a sharp corner at about 30 mph on my 85 gt and my rear end slid out and i sailed into a tree and now i can stand between my front wheels ..the moral of the story is ,at least you still have a car worth fixing ..||||reg||1
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||08-11-2000||03:13 PM||||I would like to thank you all very much! I got it into pep boys for an alignment. They couldnt do it because of a bent inner tie rod  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. You were all pretty much right about the tie rod being bent. But im ordering a new tie rod now from the fiero store and getting it installed in a few days with an alignment. Then i should be back to normal.<P>Once again thank you all so much for your support and experties!||||reg||7
